# =============================================================================
# WHO I AM on the Schonfeld estate. The corporate login, declared ONCE.
#
# This is the only person-specific value in the whole config: every IdentityFile
# is a machine-agnostic ~/.ssh/<name> path, so the username is all that changes
# between people.
#
# A DIFFERENT PERSON using this repo:
#   1. cp -r ssh/shared/thanujan ssh/shared/<their-name>
#   2. edit the User line below, and the git IdentityFile lines if they differ
#   3. in ssh/<platform>/<machine>/config, swap the two
#      Include ~/shellrc/ssh/shared/thanujan/... lines for their directory
# Nothing under ssh/shared/work/ needs to change - it holds no usernames.
#
# Included BEFORE shared/work/, so a value here beats anything there. For a
# ONE-OFF difference on a single box, use ssh/local/*.config instead: it is
# included ahead of even this, and is git-ignored.
#
# Hosts deliberately NOT listed here, because they log in as something else:
#   sf_bench_svc_dshare_p (svc_dshare_p)   SF_SANDBOX, dev-alchmy (ec2-user)
#   bench-dev-thanush (thanumahee)         bench-dev-stag (bench)
#   github*/gitlab* (git)
# The alchmy_ny5p* pattern covers the _svcP/_svcU variants too: you log in as
# yourself and sudo afterwards, which is what their RemoteCommand does.
# =============================================================================
Host sf_jump sf_bench sf_databricks_dev sf_databricks_prod alchmy_ny5p* slidev sliprod cwiq_pipe08 data_migration_dev_server edpces03 ny5-pr-edpces-03
  User bthanujan.mahendran
